    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "This mid-terraced, two-storey house, with a garden to the rear & double drive to the front, presents an excellent opportunity for buyers seeking to establish a home within a mature and established community.\r\nIdeally located this property is within comfortable walking distance of the town’s schools and is also conveniently close to the town centre, leisure centre and Cobh Connect bus stop, offering frequent services to and from Cork City.\r\n\r\nCombining a convenient location with excellent transport links and a well-established residential setting, this property offers an ideal opportunity for first-time buyers, families or those looking to make their home in a mature community.\r\n\r\nThe property achieves an energy rating better than typically expected for a home of this size, age and specification, benefiting from a number of energy-efficient upgrades. These include a high-efficiency condensing gas boiler, thermostatic radiator valves (TRVs), replacement windows to the front, attic insulation and pumped cavity wall insulation.\r\n\r\nThese improvements contribute to enhanced energy efficiency, improved heat retention and potentially lower heating costs, while adding to the overall comfort of the home.\r\n\r\nThe property has been vacant for two years & the purchaser may qualify for the vacant property refurbishment grant."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Excellent location Close to all amenities \r\nDouble driveway to the front\r\nEnclosed rear garden\r\nMature well established estate\r\nBus stop directly across from the estate\r\nAttic insulated \r\nPumped cavity wall insulation"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
